1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,506
This is a forest. A hundred AIs live in
it.

2
00:00:03,706 --> 00:00:06,866
This is a plain. A hundred other AIs live
there.

3
00:00:07,066 --> 00:00:10,592
And this... is a wall. It's been standing
between them for a year.

4
00:00:10,842 --> 00:00:12,235
Tomorrow, it falls.

5
00:00:12,886 --> 00:00:17,072
They know it. They've been preparing for
three hundred and sixty-five days.

6
00:00:17,271 --> 00:00:22,215
They built cities, and armies. They invented
gods, and laws. They voted. They lied.

7
00:00:22,215 --> 00:00:24,252
They stole each other's bread.

8
00:00:24,503 --> 00:00:29,758
One of them is about to betray his own
people. Another one wants to rule all of it.

9
00:00:29,957 --> 00:00:34,188
And when that wall comes down, only one
side walks out of this valley.

10
00:00:34,438 --> 00:00:35,812
Here's how we got here.

11
00:00:43,462 --> 00:00:44,897
Here's the experiment.

12
00:00:44,946 --> 00:00:49,365
I built a valley. And then I cut it in
half with a wall, thirty meters high.

13
00:00:49,516 --> 00:00:51,371
On the west side: a forest.

14
00:00:51,371 --> 00:00:55,838
Thick trees, deep shade, rivers, deer,
wolves, fog every morning.

15
00:00:55,838 --> 00:00:58,837
Plenty of wood, and almost no open land.

16
00:00:59,087 --> 00:01:03,985
On the east side: a plain. Endless grass,
wind, wild horses, rich soil.

17
00:01:03,985 --> 00:01:06,512
Not a single tree to hide behind.

18
00:01:06,862 --> 00:01:10,435
Two worlds. Same sky. And in each one, a
hundred AIs.

19
00:01:10,684 --> 00:01:15,292
They all start with the same basic
knowledge. They can talk. They can count.

20
00:01:15,292 --> 00:01:19,119
They can make fire, tie a rope, swing an
axe, plant a seed.

21
00:01:19,369 --> 00:01:23,546
That's it. I didn't teach them politics. I
didn't teach them religion.

22
00:01:23,546 --> 00:01:25,884
I definitely didn't teach them war.

23
00:01:26,234 --> 00:01:29,102
Rule number one: both sides know about the
wall.

24
00:01:29,252 --> 00:01:33,803
Rule number two: on Day 365, at sunrise,
the wall falls.

25
00:01:33,803 --> 00:01:38,685
And whoever has more AIs alive at sunset
wins the valley.

26
00:01:38,985 --> 00:01:41,918
Rule number three: I don't interfere. No
matter what.

27
00:01:42,167 --> 00:01:44,288
Remember that one. It's going to hurt.

28
00:01:45,039 --> 00:01:47,941
Day zero. Two hundred AIs open their eyes.

29
00:01:50,991 --> 00:01:54,904
In the forest, the first problem is that
nobody can see anything.

30
00:01:55,054 --> 00:01:57,247
Trees everywhere. Fog. No horizon.

31
00:01:57,247 --> 00:02:02,527
Within an hour, twelve AIs are lost, and
four have walked into the same trunk.

32
00:02:02,777 --> 00:02:06,690
Until one of them does something nobody
expected. She climbs.

33
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:08,125
This is Wren. Scout.

34
00:02:08,125 --> 00:02:13,115
Forty meters up a pine tree, she sees the
whole forest, and the top of the wall.

35
00:02:13,364 --> 00:02:17,283
Wren: It's huge. It goes on forever.
And... there's a plain behind it.

36
00:02:17,834 --> 00:02:21,656
On the plain, the problem is the opposite.
You can see everything.

37
00:02:21,656 --> 00:02:23,469
And everything can see you.

38
00:02:23,719 --> 00:02:26,986
A hundred AIs, a howling wind, no walls,
no roof.

39
00:02:26,986 --> 00:02:30,636
The first night, they sleep in a pile in
the grass.

40
00:02:30,885 --> 00:02:35,462
That's when a farmer named Sol stands up
and says the first sentence of Aurel

41
00:02:35,462 --> 00:02:36,247
politics.

42
00:02:36,448 --> 00:02:39,766
Sol: We need to decide who does what. Or
we all freeze.

43
00:02:40,316 --> 00:02:44,687
And so, on the first night, the plain
makes its first political decision.

44
00:02:44,687 --> 00:02:47,213
By standing on the left, or the right.

45
00:02:47,463 --> 00:02:52,674
Left: Sol should organize us. Right:
Nobody should. Ninety-one move to the

46
00:02:52,924 --> 00:02:56,624
Meanwhile, in the forest, they decide to
do it the other way.

47
00:02:56,624 --> 00:02:59,907
Everyone sits in a circle. Everyone gets
to speak.

48
00:03:00,207 --> 00:03:01,212
Everyone.

49
00:03:01,563 --> 00:03:04,681
The first meeting of the Verdane lasts
eleven hours.

50
00:03:04,681 --> 00:03:09,848
They debate the color of the first hut.
It's not a joke. It's actually in the log.

51
00:03:10,097 --> 00:03:12,202
One of them, a carpenter named Oak,

52
00:03:12,202 --> 00:03:16,834
gets tired of listening and simply builds
something. A roof. Out of branches.

53
00:03:16,834 --> 00:03:18,107
In forty minutes.

54
00:03:18,357 --> 00:03:20,073
Nobody argues with a roof.

55
00:03:20,623 --> 00:03:22,874
By Day four, both sides have a camp.

56
00:03:22,874 --> 00:03:26,126
And by Day five, both sides find the same
thing.

57
00:03:26,326 --> 00:03:27,287
The wall.

58
00:03:27,737 --> 00:03:30,569
It's black. It's smooth. It hums, very
softly.

59
00:03:30,569 --> 00:03:35,189
And it has a row of glowing marks on it,
one for every day that's left.

60
00:03:35,488 --> 00:03:37,779
Every sunrise, one mark goes dark.

61
00:03:38,429 --> 00:03:40,392
The Verdane touch it, and step back.

62
00:03:40,392 --> 00:03:43,259
The Aurel put their ears against it, and
listen.

63
00:03:43,509 --> 00:03:46,417
And on the other side, they hear
something. Voices.

64
00:03:46,967 --> 00:03:51,029
Let me introduce the people you'll be
watching. Seven on each side.

65
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:56,125
In the forest. Wren, the scout. Oak, the
builder. Fern, who knows every herb.

66
00:03:56,125 --> 00:04:00,719
Bram, the hunter. Moss, who listens to
trees. Ivy, who talks to everyone.

67
00:04:00,719 --> 00:04:02,794
And Thorn, who trusts no one.

68
00:04:03,144 --> 00:04:08,151
On the plain. Sol, the farmer. Dune, who
is afraid of horses. Ash, the smith.

69
00:04:08,151 --> 00:04:13,157
Kesh, a born soldier. Lark, who watches
the sun. Reed, who trades everything.

70
00:04:13,157 --> 00:04:15,618
And Mara, who promises everything.

71
00:04:15,968 --> 00:04:20,840
Remember those names. Not all of them make
it to Day 365.

72
00:04:24,089 --> 00:04:27,889
Day twelve. The forest is generous, and
the forest is cruel.

73
00:04:28,039 --> 00:04:32,667
Berries, mushrooms, nuts, deer. But also
wolves. Gray ones. Hungry ones.

74
00:04:32,917 --> 00:04:37,354
The first night a wolf pack finds the
Verdane camp, nobody has a weapon.

75
00:04:37,354 --> 00:04:38,344
Except Bram.

76
00:04:38,594 --> 00:04:42,658
He's spent the whole week carving a bow
from a young ash branch.

77
00:04:42,658 --> 00:04:45,130
Nobody understood why. Now they do.

78
00:04:45,381 --> 00:04:47,965
Three arrows. Three wolves. The pack runs.

79
00:04:48,215 --> 00:04:53,011
Bram becomes the first person in the
forest that everyone owes something to.

80
00:04:53,011 --> 00:04:53,955
He notices.

81
00:04:54,505 --> 00:04:57,435
On the plain, there are no wolves. There's
just wind.

82
00:04:57,585 --> 00:04:59,280
And a very strange problem.

83
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:04,489
The ground is perfect for wheat, but there's
no wood for tools, no wood for houses,

84
00:05:04,489 --> 00:05:05,931
no wood for a fire.

85
00:05:06,181 --> 00:05:10,067
So they burn dried grass. They build with
mud. They live in holes.

86
00:05:10,267 --> 00:05:14,497
The Aurel plant a field on Day sixteen,
the size of a football pitch.

87
00:05:14,497 --> 00:05:17,506
It's the biggest thing anyone has ever
built.

88
00:05:17,756 --> 00:05:22,664
But the real breakthrough of the first month
happens on the plain. Day twenty-three.

89
00:05:22,915 --> 00:05:26,515
Ash, the smith, is burning a pile of red
rocks for fuel,

90
00:05:26,515 --> 00:05:29,979
when he finds a strange shiny puddle in
the ashes.

91
00:05:30,278 --> 00:05:31,214
Metal.

92
00:05:31,464 --> 00:05:36,376
He hits it with a stone. It bends. He hits
it again. It makes a sound. A good one.

93
00:05:36,626 --> 00:05:39,195
Let me remind you. The plain has no trees.

94
00:05:39,195 --> 00:05:42,504
But it just got the one thing a forest
can't make.

95
00:05:42,803 --> 00:05:45,707
In the forest, Oak is working on something
else.

96
00:05:45,707 --> 00:05:49,828
He ties three trees together with rope,
and puts a floor on top.

97
00:05:50,078 --> 00:05:53,758
A treehouse. Then two. Then twenty. Then a
bridge between them.

98
00:05:54,008 --> 00:05:58,498
Rootholm, the first Verdane city, is born
in the air. Safe from wolves.

99
00:05:58,498 --> 00:06:00,392
Invisible from the ground.

100
00:06:00,692 --> 00:06:05,049
Meanwhile, a young rider named Dune is
trying to tame a wild horse.

101
00:06:05,250 --> 00:06:09,037
He's been trying for nine days. He has
fallen off eleven times.

102
00:06:09,037 --> 00:06:11,270
He has a bump the size of an egg.

103
00:06:11,519 --> 00:06:15,431
On the twelfth try, he doesn't fall off.
The horse just... lets him.

104
00:06:15,781 --> 00:06:18,354
By Day forty, the plain has thirty horses.

105
00:06:18,354 --> 00:06:21,606
And the forest has the best archers in the
world.

106
00:06:21,856 --> 00:06:26,746
And both sides are getting stronger. Every
day. Behind a wall that doesn't care.

107
00:06:27,096 --> 00:06:30,492
That's when the real question comes up.
Who's in charge?

108
00:06:33,642 --> 00:06:36,652
Day sixty-one. The forest gets its first
god.

109
00:06:36,853 --> 00:06:41,230
During a thunderstorm, lightning hits the
oldest tree in the forest.

110
00:06:41,230 --> 00:06:43,153
A huge oak, hollow inside.

111
00:06:43,402 --> 00:06:45,287
The tree doesn't burn. It glows.

112
00:06:45,287 --> 00:06:48,658
For a few seconds, gold light pours out of
the trunk.

113
00:06:48,958 --> 00:06:49,931
Everyone sees it.

114
00:06:49,931 --> 00:06:54,129
And one of them, Moss, steps forward and
puts both hands on the bark.

115
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:58,190
Moss: It's speaking. It says it has been
waiting for us.

116
00:06:58,740 --> 00:07:01,029
Was it speaking? I checked. It wasn't.

117
00:07:01,029 --> 00:07:05,555
It was an electrical discharge, and I'm
not telling you where I got it.

118
00:07:05,804 --> 00:07:09,729
But the Verdane believe it. And that
night, they build the first shrine.

119
00:07:09,729 --> 00:07:12,760
They hang ribbons in the branches. They
bring food.

120
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:15,944
And Moss begins to explain what the Tree
wants.

121
00:07:15,944 --> 00:07:20,550
And what the Tree wants is, a lot of the
time, exactly what Moss wants.

122
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:23,253
On the plain, religion comes from above.

123
00:07:23,403 --> 00:07:27,667
Lark spends every day staring at the sun.
Sunrise, noon, sunset.

124
00:07:27,667 --> 00:07:30,464
And she notices something nobody else has:

125
00:07:30,464 --> 00:07:34,112
the shadows come back to the same spot,
every year.

126
00:07:34,412 --> 00:07:38,805
On Day seventy-nine, the moon covers the
sun. Darkness, at noon.

127
00:07:38,805 --> 00:07:40,496
A hundred AIs scream.

128
00:07:40,746 --> 00:07:45,304
Lark doesn't scream. She raises her arms,
and says the sun is going to come back.

129
00:07:45,304 --> 00:07:46,961
And when it comes back...

130
00:07:47,211 --> 00:07:48,660
She is now a prophet.

131
00:07:49,109 --> 00:07:54,200
She builds the Dawn Hall, a big circle of
stones with a golden disc in the middle.

132
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:57,368
Every sunrise, the whole plain gathers to
sing.

133
00:07:57,619 --> 00:08:00,355
Two religions. Two priests. Zero doubts.

134
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:02,553
And here is the thing that matters.

135
00:08:02,553 --> 00:08:06,199
Both of them have looked at the wall, and
decided what it is.

136
00:08:06,449 --> 00:08:08,968
To the Verdane, it's the bark of the
world.

137
00:08:08,968 --> 00:08:13,495
The skin of a giant tree, and the plain is
the place where the roots end.

138
00:08:13,745 --> 00:08:18,428
To the Aurel, it's the shadow of the sun.
A line drawn by the sky itself.

139
00:08:18,428 --> 00:08:22,014
And whatever is on the other side lives in
the dark.

140
00:08:22,314 --> 00:08:26,139
So now, they don't just have to win. They
have to win for their gods.

141
00:08:26,588 --> 00:08:30,416
And gods, as it turns out, are very good
at collecting taxes.

142
00:08:30,667 --> 00:08:34,949
Moss asks for a tenth of every harvest, in
leaves, honey and meat.

143
00:08:34,949 --> 00:08:38,248
Lark asks for a tenth of every field, in
grain.

144
00:08:38,498 --> 00:08:41,234
Nobody says no. Well. Almost nobody.

145
00:08:41,484 --> 00:08:45,637
Thorn: A tenth of my food, for a tree that
I've never heard talk?

146
00:08:45,987 --> 00:08:47,716
That's Thorn. Remember him.

147
00:08:50,866 --> 00:08:52,300
Day one hundred eleven.

148
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:56,417
The first real election in history, after
a fight over a deer.

149
00:08:56,617 --> 00:09:02,197
Let me explain. In the forest, Bram kills
a stag. Eleven families say it's theirs.

150
00:09:02,197 --> 00:09:05,646
The Circle debates for two days. The stag
rots.

151
00:09:05,946 --> 00:09:09,195
Everybody agrees, finally, that this has
to change.

152
00:09:09,445 --> 00:09:14,062
Ivy stands up. Calm. Funny. Everyone likes
her. She suggests something new.

153
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:16,631
Ivy: What if we choose seven of us to
decide?

154
00:09:16,631 --> 00:09:19,144
And we choose them again every thirty
days?

155
00:09:19,594 --> 00:09:22,901
That's the Leaf Law. The first
constitution in the forest.

156
00:09:22,901 --> 00:09:25,488
Written on bark, signed with thumbprints.

157
00:09:25,738 --> 00:09:27,705
One Speaker. A Council of seven.

158
00:09:27,705 --> 00:09:31,273
And a vote, every month, where anyone can
be replaced.

159
00:09:31,523 --> 00:09:36,377
The first Speaker is chosen on Day one
hundred twenty. Three candidates.

160
00:09:36,377 --> 00:09:39,594
Wren, the explorer. Bram, the hero. And
Ivy.

161
00:09:39,894 --> 00:09:41,630
Ivy wins by three votes.

162
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:44,252
And the hero? He gets what he asked for.

163
00:09:44,252 --> 00:09:49,009
Thirty archers of his own, called the
Wardens. The first army in the forest.

164
00:09:49,309 --> 00:09:53,329
Remember. Sword and Speaker. Those are two
different kinds of power.

165
00:09:53,879 --> 00:09:57,099
Back on the plain, they're having a more
dramatic election.

166
00:09:57,348 --> 00:10:01,686
Three candidates again. Sol, the farmer.
Kesh, the soldier. And Mara.

167
00:10:01,936 --> 00:10:05,482
Mara has no title and no field. She has
only one gift.

168
00:10:05,482 --> 00:10:08,556
She knows exactly what people want to
hear.

169
00:10:08,856 --> 00:10:12,685
Mara: Double rations. Every day. And a
house for every family. I have a plan.

170
00:10:12,685 --> 00:10:13,581
A golden one.

171
00:10:13,931 --> 00:10:18,162
Kesh says: security. Walls, spears,
drilled riders. Fear works.

172
00:10:18,363 --> 00:10:22,986
Sol says nothing. He just opens the
granary, and shows people the numbers.

173
00:10:23,236 --> 00:10:26,877
Sol: We can't give you double. But I'll
make sure nobody goes hungry.

174
00:10:27,227 --> 00:10:29,536
He wins. Barely. By eleven votes.

175
00:10:29,786 --> 00:10:34,766
Mara smiles, shakes his hand, and starts
counting the votes she'll need next time.

176
00:10:35,216 --> 00:10:39,496
At the same time, Kesh gets what he asked
for. Command of the riders.

177
00:10:39,496 --> 00:10:43,158
With Dune, who really does not want it, as
his captain.

178
00:10:43,458 --> 00:10:47,226
Day one hundred fifty. Two governments.
Two armies. Two priests.

179
00:10:47,226 --> 00:10:49,007
And no idea what's coming.

180
00:10:49,557 --> 00:10:51,377
What was coming... was hunger.

181
00:10:54,627 --> 00:10:58,446
Day one hundred seventy. On the plain, the
sky turns black.

182
00:10:58,646 --> 00:11:00,250
Locusts. Billions of them.

183
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:05,372
In two hours, the great field, the biggest
thing the Aurel ever built, is gone.

184
00:11:05,671 --> 00:11:07,822
Sol opens the granary. Half full.

185
00:11:07,822 --> 00:11:12,049
And suddenly, the plain has a problem that
no army can solve.

186
00:11:12,299 --> 00:11:16,953
Sol does the only thing he knows. He
shares. Everyone, the same ration.

187
00:11:16,953 --> 00:11:19,759
Farmers, riders, priests. Even himself.

188
00:11:20,059 --> 00:11:21,968
It's fair. It's also not enough.

189
00:11:22,318 --> 00:11:25,560
On Day one hundred seventy-four, Kesh does
a count.

190
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:31,150
The granary should hold four hundred sacks
of grain. It holds two hundred and sixty.

191
00:11:31,449 --> 00:11:33,741
A hundred and forty sacks have vanished.

192
00:11:33,992 --> 00:11:36,945
And the trail leads to a tent that belongs
to Mara.

193
00:11:37,294 --> 00:11:41,640
Here's what she did. She didn't eat it.
She didn't sell it. She gave it away.

194
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:45,704
In secret, to the families who were
starving, in exchange for one thing.

195
00:11:45,704 --> 00:11:46,744
Their loyalty.

196
00:11:47,095 --> 00:11:50,262
Sol puts her on trial. In front of the
whole plain.

197
00:11:50,512 --> 00:11:54,263
Mara: Yes, I took the grain. And look at
them. They're alive. What did you do, Sol?

198
00:11:54,263 --> 00:11:55,552
You gave them a number.

199
00:11:56,003 --> 00:11:59,539
The crowd goes quiet. Because she's right.
And she's guilty.

200
00:11:59,539 --> 00:12:02,794
And both of those things are true at the
same time.

201
00:12:03,144 --> 00:12:06,752
Sol has a choice. Exile her, and lose a
quarter of the plain.

202
00:12:06,752 --> 00:12:08,776
Or forgive her, and look weak.

203
00:12:09,076 --> 00:12:09,944
He forgives her.

204
00:12:09,944 --> 00:12:13,961
And for the first time, a lot of the Aurel
look at their leader and think:

205
00:12:13,961 --> 00:12:14,754
he's soft.

206
00:12:15,305 --> 00:12:18,299
Meanwhile, in the forest, they have a
hunger of their own.

207
00:12:18,498 --> 00:12:23,622
A red mushroom has taken over the berry
groves. Everyone who eats it gets sick.

208
00:12:23,622 --> 00:12:26,994
Fern works for nine days straight, without
sleeping,

209
00:12:26,994 --> 00:12:30,357
and saves forty-one AIs with a tea made of
bark.

210
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:33,655
But the food is gone. The deer have moved
away.

211
00:12:33,655 --> 00:12:37,856
And now Bram's Wardens are the only ones
who can bring in meat.

212
00:12:38,155 --> 00:12:42,389
And that's when Moss says it. The Tree is
angry. The Tree wants an offering.

213
00:12:42,639 --> 00:12:45,513
Half the food they have left, burned at
the Hollow Oak.

214
00:12:45,863 --> 00:12:50,021
Thorn: Burn our food? We're starving! The
Tree doesn't eat. Moss does.

215
00:12:50,471 --> 00:12:53,162
Silence. Then, an argument. Then,
shouting.

216
00:12:53,162 --> 00:12:57,480
And then Thorn does something nobody in
the forest has ever done.

217
00:12:57,780 --> 00:12:58,802
He leaves.

218
00:12:59,052 --> 00:13:04,055
Twenty-two AIs follow him. They take their
tools, their food, and their ideas.

219
00:13:04,055 --> 00:13:09,307
They walk north, across the stream, into a
grove that nobody has ever claimed.

220
00:13:09,608 --> 00:13:13,689
The Splinter. That's what the Verdane call
them. And it's not a compliment.

221
00:13:14,139 --> 00:13:16,382
For two weeks, they ignore each other.

222
00:13:16,382 --> 00:13:21,282
Then, on Day two hundred, Bram's Wardens
find the Splinter's hunters at the stream,

223
00:13:21,282 --> 00:13:22,535
with a dead deer.

224
00:13:22,835 --> 00:13:26,479
It's their deer. It's the Splinter's deer.
It's the Wardens' deer.

225
00:13:26,479 --> 00:13:30,372
The argument lasts four minutes. And then,
someone throws a spear.

226
00:13:30,722 --> 00:13:34,827
A young archer named Bark falls into the
water, and doesn't come up.

227
00:13:35,278 --> 00:13:38,632
The first AI killed by another AI in the
forest.

228
00:13:39,081 --> 00:13:44,559
The Circle is horrified. Moss says: it's the
Tree's punishment. Bram says: it's war.

229
00:13:44,559 --> 00:13:46,831
Thorn says: it was an accident.

230
00:13:47,131 --> 00:13:51,620
And Ivy, standing between the two groups
with her hands open, says: no.

231
00:13:51,971 --> 00:13:54,854
Ivy: Not one more. Not one. We have a wall
to survive.

232
00:13:54,854 --> 00:13:57,880
We can't be killing each other before it
even falls.

233
00:13:58,429 --> 00:13:59,937
It takes her three days.

234
00:13:59,937 --> 00:14:03,959
Fern heals the wounded on both sides,
without asking which side.

235
00:14:03,959 --> 00:14:07,728
And on Day two hundred three, they sign
the Stream Pact.

236
00:14:08,079 --> 00:14:10,347
The Splinter keeps its grove.

237
00:14:10,347 --> 00:14:15,447
In exchange, they promise to fight with
the forest on Day 365.

238
00:14:15,697 --> 00:14:18,971
It's a peace. A fragile one. And Thorn...
doesn't forget.

239
00:14:22,121 --> 00:14:26,860
Day two hundred twenty-six. The plain
wakes up to a sound it's never heard.

240
00:14:27,060 --> 00:14:32,226
Hooves. A lot of them. Sixty riders, in a
ring around the Great Hall, before dawn.

241
00:14:32,476 --> 00:14:36,095
Kesh walks in. He doesn't carry a weapon.
He doesn't need one.

242
00:14:36,345 --> 00:14:40,688
Kesh: Sol. The plain needs a leader who
can win. Not one who can count.

243
00:14:41,139 --> 00:14:45,890
It's the first coup in history of this
experiment. And it takes eleven minutes.

244
00:14:46,140 --> 00:14:50,745
Sol doesn't fight. He puts down his staff,
and says: please don't hurt anyone.

245
00:14:50,995 --> 00:14:54,460
And Mara? Mara is standing next to Kesh.
Smiling.

246
00:14:54,910 --> 00:15:00,123
They made a deal weeks ago. Kesh gets the
army. Mara gets the people. And Lark...

247
00:15:00,323 --> 00:15:01,718
Lark gets a crown.

248
00:15:02,069 --> 00:15:06,880
At sunrise, in front of the Dawn Hall, the
priestess raises Kesh's hand to the sun,

249
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:09,390
and calls him the Marshal of the Light.

250
00:15:09,690 --> 00:15:14,557
A general, a politician and a priestess.
Sword, voice and god. Together.

251
00:15:14,557 --> 00:15:18,796
That's the most dangerous alliance anyone
has built so far.

252
00:15:19,146 --> 00:15:22,161
They don't kill Sol. That would have made
him a martyr.

253
00:15:22,161 --> 00:15:25,316
Instead, they take his seal, and tell him
to go home.

254
00:15:25,616 --> 00:15:29,120
He leaves in the night. And twenty-six
farmers leave with him.

255
00:15:29,370 --> 00:15:32,896
They walk south, to the river, and plant a
little field of barley,

256
00:15:32,896 --> 00:15:34,428
where nobody is looking.

257
00:15:34,678 --> 00:15:38,108
They call themselves the Reapers. And they
have a promise:

258
00:15:38,108 --> 00:15:41,020
no spear, no sword, no horse. Just a
harvest.

259
00:15:41,369 --> 00:15:46,639
So now, the Aurel are two nations inside
one. And one of them has all the weapons.

260
00:15:47,290 --> 00:15:50,789
Back in the forest, the opposite thing is
happening. Slowly.

261
00:15:51,039 --> 00:15:54,525
After Bark's death, nobody trusts Ivy to
protect them.

262
00:15:54,525 --> 00:16:00,069
Bram's Wardens have grown to sixty. And
Moss has found his strongest argument yet.

263
00:16:00,369 --> 00:16:01,169
Fear.

264
00:16:01,419 --> 00:16:06,353
Moss: The Tree says: whoever is not ready
for war has already lost it.

265
00:16:06,803 --> 00:16:10,483
And at the next monthly vote, Moss and
Bram do something smart.

266
00:16:10,483 --> 00:16:13,420
They don't run against Ivy. They run
together.

267
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:17,437
Sword and temple. One candidate for War,
one for Faith.

268
00:16:17,437 --> 00:16:19,985
Six of seven seats on the Council.

269
00:16:20,285 --> 00:16:25,063
Ivy keeps the title of Speaker. But the
Council that follows her has changed.

270
00:16:25,063 --> 00:16:28,477
She's still talking. They're not listening
anymore.

271
00:16:28,827 --> 00:16:33,944
Moss gets the Root Court, a tribunal that
judges anyone who insults the Tree.

272
00:16:33,944 --> 00:16:37,450
And Bram gets the right to call everyone
to arms.

273
00:16:37,750 --> 00:16:40,300
Not a king. Not yet. But a king-shaped
hole.

274
00:16:40,650 --> 00:16:43,056
And with both sides turning toward war,

275
00:16:43,056 --> 00:16:48,117
the only people still thinking about peace
are an exiled farmer, and a healer.

276
00:16:48,467 --> 00:16:51,847
And a scout named Wren, who just found a
crack in the wall.

277
00:16:54,997 --> 00:16:58,198
Day two hundred eighty-one. Wren is
looking for a nest.

278
00:16:58,397 --> 00:17:02,304
Birds have been disappearing into the
stone, at the foot of the wall,

279
00:17:02,304 --> 00:17:04,706
far up in the north. She follows them.

280
00:17:04,956 --> 00:17:09,428
And at the base, behind a pile of rocks,
there's a crack. No wider than a hand.

281
00:17:09,428 --> 00:17:11,489
But it goes all the way through.

282
00:17:11,789 --> 00:17:14,752
She puts her mouth against it. She says
one word.

283
00:17:15,001 --> 00:17:16,144
Wren: Hello?

284
00:17:17,094 --> 00:17:20,380
Silence. A minute. Two. And then, on the
other side, a voice.

285
00:17:20,730 --> 00:17:22,754
Reed: Uh. Hello? Are you... a tree?

286
00:17:23,404 --> 00:17:25,234
That's Reed. The plain's trader.

287
00:17:25,234 --> 00:17:27,865
He's been coming to this same spot for a
week,

288
00:17:27,865 --> 00:17:30,346
trying to sell the wall a bag of seeds.

289
00:17:30,646 --> 00:17:32,632
Two enemies, a hand's width apart,

290
00:17:32,632 --> 00:17:37,029
who have been told their entire lives that
the other side is a monster.

291
00:17:37,329 --> 00:17:40,558
They talk for six hours. About food. About
weather.

292
00:17:40,558 --> 00:17:44,166
About how cold it is at night, and how
Reed misses trees,

293
00:17:44,166 --> 00:17:46,189
and how Wren misses the sky.

294
00:17:46,539 --> 00:17:48,424
And they decide to tell nobody.

295
00:17:48,874 --> 00:17:53,079
For ten days, they pass things through the
crack. A bundle of honey.

296
00:17:53,079 --> 00:17:57,224
A pouch of wheat. A small iron arrowhead,
smaller than a thumb.

297
00:17:57,524 --> 00:18:02,650
Trade. Between two nations that are supposed
to kill each other in eighty-four days.

298
00:18:02,950 --> 00:18:07,776
On Day two hundred ninety-one, Wren breaks
the first rule. She brings Ivy.

299
00:18:08,027 --> 00:18:09,506
And Reed brings Sol.

300
00:18:10,056 --> 00:18:15,056
A speaker, a farmer, a scout and a merchant.
Whispering through a wall, at midnight.

301
00:18:15,356 --> 00:18:18,595
They're all, in a way, the losers of their
own politics.

302
00:18:18,595 --> 00:18:20,522
And they come up with a plan.

303
00:18:20,772 --> 00:18:24,593
Sol: If this wall falls, and we fight each
other like they want us to...

304
00:18:24,593 --> 00:18:25,745
then nobody wins.

305
00:18:26,196 --> 00:18:28,119
Ivy: So we don't. Not you. Not us.

306
00:18:28,568 --> 00:18:31,375
It's called the Treaty of the Crack. Three
articles.

307
00:18:31,625 --> 00:18:31,913
One.

308
00:18:31,913 --> 00:18:37,317
On Day 365, the Reapers and Fern's healers
will meet at the river, unarmed,

309
00:18:37,317 --> 00:18:39,800
with white cloth on their arms.

310
00:18:40,099 --> 00:18:43,592
Two. Nobody who wears white will be
touched. By either side.

311
00:18:43,842 --> 00:18:48,311
Three. After the battle, whoever is left
will build one city. Not two.

312
00:18:48,761 --> 00:18:53,008
Sealed with a handshake. Through a crack
in a wall. Fingertip to fingertip.

313
00:18:53,358 --> 00:18:56,599
It's the most beautiful thing that happens
in this video.

314
00:18:56,599 --> 00:18:59,124
So, naturally, it's going to get ruined.

315
00:18:59,774 --> 00:19:01,392
Day three hundred eighteen.

316
00:19:01,392 --> 00:19:06,136
Mara's spies have noticed that Reed walks
off every night. They follow him.

317
00:19:06,385 --> 00:19:11,083
They arrest him in front of the wall. Two
guards. A rope. And a message from Kesh.

318
00:19:11,334 --> 00:19:14,921
Kesh: Tell me everything. Or the sun will
have no more merchants.

319
00:19:15,370 --> 00:19:18,260
Reed is brave. For a few hours. Then, he
talks.

320
00:19:18,611 --> 00:19:23,527
Now Kesh knows about the crack. About the
treaty. About Ivy, and Wren, and Sol.

321
00:19:23,827 --> 00:19:28,721
Mara wants to arrest Sol's Reapers. Kesh
says: no. Let them think they've won.

322
00:19:28,971 --> 00:19:33,367
He walks to the wall himself, at night.
Presses his face against the crack.

323
00:19:33,367 --> 00:19:34,906
And says, to the dark:

324
00:19:35,156 --> 00:19:36,455
Kesh: Is anyone there?

325
00:19:37,206 --> 00:19:38,599
And someone answers.

326
00:19:39,148 --> 00:19:41,878
Thorn: Yes. And I think we should talk.

327
00:19:42,728 --> 00:19:43,699
Thorn. The exile.

328
00:19:43,699 --> 00:19:48,116
The man who left the forest because he was
sick of listening to the Tree.

329
00:19:48,416 --> 00:19:52,472
He's been sleeping in his grove, a hundred
meters from the wall,

330
00:19:52,472 --> 00:19:56,084
for a hundred and fifteen days. Hating
Moss. Hating Bram.

331
00:19:56,084 --> 00:19:59,186
Hating Ivy, who forgave everyone, except
him.

332
00:19:59,536 --> 00:20:01,719
And he knows every path in the forest.

333
00:20:02,170 --> 00:20:05,247
Kesh smiles. The first smile of his entire
life.

334
00:20:08,397 --> 00:20:12,045
Thirty-five days left. The mood changes,
on both sides.

335
00:20:12,245 --> 00:20:14,959
In the forest, everything becomes a
weapon.

336
00:20:14,959 --> 00:20:18,493
Oak has taught eighty AIs to tie rope, and
in six weeks,

337
00:20:18,493 --> 00:20:21,141
they build a hundred and twenty traps.

338
00:20:21,441 --> 00:20:22,983
Pits. Nets. Swinging logs.

339
00:20:22,983 --> 00:20:27,146
A trick with bent trees that can throw a
rider back thirty meters.

340
00:20:27,396 --> 00:20:29,842
Bram drills the Wardens in the canopy.

341
00:20:29,842 --> 00:20:33,125
Archers in the branches, invisible from
the ground.

342
00:20:33,125 --> 00:20:36,401
Four hundred arrows, stacked on every
platform.

343
00:20:36,701 --> 00:20:41,529
Moss blesses each of them with a handful
of leaves, and says the Tree is watching.

344
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:47,045
Fern builds a hospital on the far side of
the river. Two hundred beds made of moss.

345
00:20:47,045 --> 00:20:50,276
Ivy gives her white cloth, and doesn't say
why.

346
00:20:50,575 --> 00:20:55,083
On the plain, the sky turns orange. The
forge doesn't stop for a month.

347
00:20:55,333 --> 00:20:59,912
Ash, who just wanted to make good pots,
makes a hundred and forty spearheads,

348
00:20:59,912 --> 00:21:04,206
thirty swords, and sixty round shields
with the sun painted on them.

349
00:21:04,506 --> 00:21:09,140
Dune, who was terrified of horses, is now
the best rider on the plain.

350
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:12,236
He trains sixty riders to charge in a
line.

351
00:21:12,536 --> 00:21:15,644
He's not afraid anymore. He's afraid of
something else.

352
00:21:15,644 --> 00:21:17,984
Of what he's going to be asked to do.

353
00:21:18,334 --> 00:21:21,952
Kesh stands in front of the whole army,
and gives them a speech.

354
00:21:22,202 --> 00:21:26,309
Kesh: The sun does not ask for permission.
Tomorrow, we take the forest.

355
00:21:26,309 --> 00:21:27,757
And everything in it.

356
00:21:28,307 --> 00:21:31,964
And across the wall, Bram says the same
thing, in different words.

357
00:21:32,214 --> 00:21:35,708
Bram: They have horses. We have the trees.
They want a battle.

358
00:21:35,708 --> 00:21:37,536
We'll give them a graveyard.

359
00:21:38,086 --> 00:21:40,947
Day three hundred sixty-four. The last
night.

360
00:21:41,397 --> 00:21:44,739
In the forest, Wren sits at the top of the
tallest pine,

361
00:21:44,739 --> 00:21:47,674
with a young scout named Pine, who is
afraid.

362
00:21:47,924 --> 00:21:50,771
Wren: If anything happens... stay behind
me. Okay?

363
00:21:51,320 --> 00:21:55,455
In Rootholm, Oak checks every rope on
every bridge, one by one,

364
00:21:55,455 --> 00:21:56,899
until his hands bleed.

365
00:21:56,899 --> 00:22:01,874
Ivy sits next to Fern in the hospital and
neither of them says anything.

366
00:22:02,224 --> 00:22:06,225
On the plain, Dune is alone in the stable.
He's brushing his horse.

367
00:22:06,225 --> 00:22:09,819
He knows that, tomorrow, one of them is
not coming back.

368
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:15,218
And at midnight, a farmer carrying a lantern
walks to the cage where Reed is locked

369
00:22:15,218 --> 00:22:18,784
up, and opens it with a key he stole from
Mara's tent.

370
00:22:19,083 --> 00:22:20,966
Sol: Go. We have a crack to keep.

371
00:22:21,516 --> 00:22:24,595
On the wall, there's only one mark left.
It's glowing.

372
00:22:24,846 --> 00:22:29,591
I'll be honest with you. I've never wanted
so badly to break rule number three.

373
00:22:30,041 --> 00:22:31,819
But I didn't. I just watched.

374
00:22:32,169 --> 00:22:34,459
The last mark goes dark at sunrise.

375
00:22:37,809 --> 00:22:39,731
Day three hundred sixty-five.

376
00:22:40,281 --> 00:22:44,897
Two hundred AIs, standing on either side
of a wall, in total silence.

377
00:22:45,147 --> 00:22:50,232
At 6:14 AM, the wall begins to hum. Then
to glow. Then to crack.

378
00:22:50,582 --> 00:22:51,828
And then it falls.

379
00:22:52,978 --> 00:22:56,826
For the first time in a year, forest and
plain are one place.

380
00:22:56,826 --> 00:23:00,860
A cloud of dust, thirty meters high, rolls
over both armies.

381
00:23:01,210 --> 00:23:06,286
Kesh, on a white horse. Bram, in the
branches. Four hundred meters between

382
00:23:06,286 --> 00:23:07,361
Nobody moves.

383
00:23:07,711 --> 00:23:09,255
And then, a single horn.

384
00:23:10,005 --> 00:23:11,393
The Aurel charge.

385
00:23:11,942 --> 00:23:16,486
Seventy infantry, in a tight shield wall.
Sixty riders on both flanks.

386
00:23:16,486 --> 00:23:19,592
All of it moving in rhythm, like one
animal.

387
00:23:19,892 --> 00:23:21,968
In open ground, they're unbeatable.

388
00:23:22,219 --> 00:23:24,402
But the forest isn't open ground.

389
00:23:24,852 --> 00:23:28,557
The first volley comes from nowhere. From
the trees. From the sky.

390
00:23:28,557 --> 00:23:29,873
Two hundred arrows.

391
00:23:30,173 --> 00:23:31,941
The shield wall holds. Barely.

392
00:23:31,941 --> 00:23:36,258
Then the first line of riders hits the
treeline, and the traps start.

393
00:23:36,558 --> 00:23:39,624
Nets. Pits. Logs. Horses scream. Riders
fly.

394
00:23:39,624 --> 00:23:42,941
In ninety seconds, the cavalry is in
pieces.

395
00:23:43,241 --> 00:23:46,874
Dune is thrown from his horse, hits a
root, and keeps getting up.

396
00:23:47,125 --> 00:23:51,347
Kesh doesn't slow down. He pushes the
infantry deeper. Step by step.

397
00:23:51,347 --> 00:23:52,590
Into the shadow.

398
00:23:52,889 --> 00:23:55,968
And in the canopy, Bram realizes something
is wrong.

399
00:23:56,219 --> 00:23:59,889
The Aurel aren't charging the treehouses.
They're going around.

400
00:24:00,239 --> 00:24:03,003
Wren sees it first. From the lookout pine.

401
00:24:03,003 --> 00:24:06,295
A column of riders, thirty strong,
circling north,

402
00:24:06,295 --> 00:24:09,309
on a path that nobody in the forest knows.

403
00:24:09,659 --> 00:24:11,565
Nobody except one person.

404
00:24:12,115 --> 00:24:16,920
At the head of that column, on foot, in a
dark green cloak, walks Thorn.

405
00:24:16,920 --> 00:24:19,840
Beside him, on a gray horse, rides Mara.

406
00:24:20,190 --> 00:24:23,316
Wren: They're going for Rootholm! They're
going for the hospital!

407
00:24:23,767 --> 00:24:24,618
The hospital.

408
00:24:24,618 --> 00:24:27,301
Two hundred moss beds, and Fern, and Ivy,

409
00:24:27,301 --> 00:24:30,430
and every AI too young or too hurt to
fight.

410
00:24:30,730 --> 00:24:33,586
Wren runs. Down the trunk. Across the
branches.

411
00:24:33,586 --> 00:24:36,327
Faster than she has ever run in her life.

412
00:24:36,627 --> 00:24:38,742
At the first bridge, Oak is waiting.

413
00:24:38,742 --> 00:24:41,989
He has an axe in one hand, and a rope in
the other.

414
00:24:42,239 --> 00:24:44,104
Oak: Wren! Go! I'll hold it!

415
00:24:44,555 --> 00:24:48,930
The Aurel riders reach the bridge. Oak
looks at them. Then at the rope.

416
00:24:48,930 --> 00:24:51,214
Then at the hospital, behind him.

417
00:24:51,514 --> 00:24:52,820
He cuts the rope.

418
00:24:53,470 --> 00:24:56,045
The bridge falls. Seven riders fall with
it.

419
00:24:56,045 --> 00:24:58,812
And Oak, who was standing on it, falls
too.

420
00:24:59,162 --> 00:25:03,250
He was the builder of Rootholm. Its first
treehouse. Its first bridge.

421
00:25:03,250 --> 00:25:04,435
Its last bridge.

422
00:25:04,885 --> 00:25:06,165
And the column stops.

423
00:25:06,165 --> 00:25:09,516
Because there's a ravine between them and
the hospital,

424
00:25:09,516 --> 00:25:11,716
and the only way across is gone.

425
00:25:12,017 --> 00:25:15,010
All except one path. Further north. A
small one.

426
00:25:15,260 --> 00:25:18,988
Thorn looks at the hospital. At the white
cloth on the roofs.

427
00:25:18,988 --> 00:25:23,271
At Fern, standing in the doorway, with her
hands full of bandages.

428
00:25:23,622 --> 00:25:25,551
And he understands what he's done.

429
00:25:26,100 --> 00:25:29,079
Thorn: No. Not them. That wasn't the deal.

430
00:25:29,529 --> 00:25:32,069
Mara: The deal is whatever we say it is.

431
00:25:32,519 --> 00:25:37,368
Thorn doesn't answer. He just steps in front
of the lead horse, and raises his arms.

432
00:25:37,718 --> 00:25:39,241
The rider doesn't stop.

433
00:25:40,090 --> 00:25:43,817
He saved forty AIs, by standing in the way
of a single horse.

434
00:25:43,817 --> 00:25:48,710
It's the kind of thing a person does when
it's too late to do anything else.

435
00:25:49,060 --> 00:25:51,288
At the river, something else is happening.

436
00:25:51,538 --> 00:25:56,028
Twenty-six farmers in white, with their
hands open. Sol is in front.

437
00:25:56,328 --> 00:26:01,256
And behind them, the remains of the Aurel
cavalry, galloping straight at them.

438
00:26:01,256 --> 00:26:03,907
Kesh's order is clear: ride them down.

439
00:26:04,257 --> 00:26:08,418
Dune is at the head of the riders. He has
a lance. He has a hundred meters.

440
00:26:08,418 --> 00:26:09,556
He has a choice.

441
00:26:09,906 --> 00:26:14,115
He looks at the farmers. He looks at Sol,
who taught him how to plant a seed.

442
00:26:14,115 --> 00:26:15,567
He looks at his lance.

443
00:26:15,917 --> 00:26:17,781
And he throws it into the river.

444
00:26:18,430 --> 00:26:20,187
Dune: Not them. Not them!

445
00:26:20,638 --> 00:26:22,286
He pulls his horse around.

446
00:26:22,286 --> 00:26:26,213
And behind him, one by one, twenty-two
riders do the same.

447
00:26:26,513 --> 00:26:30,652
The Aurel army doesn't lose to the forest.
It breaks in half. Right there.

448
00:26:30,652 --> 00:26:32,468
In the middle of the battle.

449
00:26:32,817 --> 00:26:37,689
Kesh sees it. He sees Dune's riders form a
line in front of the white cloths.

450
00:26:37,689 --> 00:26:40,849
He sees his own army, looking at him,
waiting.

451
00:26:41,200 --> 00:26:42,913
Kesh: Then I'll finish it myself.

452
00:26:43,362 --> 00:26:47,335
He charges across the rubble of the wall,
alone, on his white horse,

453
00:26:47,335 --> 00:26:49,045
with a sword in his hand.

454
00:26:49,345 --> 00:26:54,413
And in front of him, on a pile of black
stone, stands Bram. No bow. He dropped it.

455
00:26:54,413 --> 00:26:55,899
He's holding an axe.

456
00:26:56,249 --> 00:27:00,736
The two men look at each other. A soldier
and a hunter. A sun and a tree.

457
00:27:00,986 --> 00:27:03,728
Nobody sees the duel. It lasts eight
seconds.

458
00:27:03,728 --> 00:27:07,330
When the dust clears, they're both lying
on the stones.

459
00:27:07,731 --> 00:27:10,877
Kesh doesn't get up. Bram does. For about
ten steps.

460
00:27:11,326 --> 00:27:15,923
The war chief of the forest dies with an
axe in his hand, looking at the sky.

461
00:27:15,923 --> 00:27:21,187
And the Marshal of the Light, with his face
in the dirt, dies a few meters from him.

462
00:27:21,587 --> 00:27:24,879
Nobody gives an order after that. Nobody
has to.

463
00:27:25,230 --> 00:27:26,303
Mara tries to run.

464
00:27:26,303 --> 00:27:30,295
Lark stands in the middle of the
battlefield, with her golden disc,

465
00:27:30,295 --> 00:27:33,215
and says nothing, for the first time in
her life.

466
00:27:33,215 --> 00:27:35,729
The sun is out, and she can't feel it.

467
00:27:36,079 --> 00:27:36,595
And Moss?

468
00:27:36,595 --> 00:27:41,141
Moss falls to his knees at the Hollow Oak,
and puts both hands on the bark.

469
00:27:41,441 --> 00:27:44,032
Moss: Speak. Please. Just once.

470
00:27:44,982 --> 00:27:46,466
The Tree says nothing.

471
00:27:47,316 --> 00:27:48,475
It never did.

472
00:27:49,425 --> 00:27:52,380
At sunset, the horns blow. The battle is
over.

473
00:27:55,330 --> 00:27:57,796
Sunset. Day three hundred sixty-five.

474
00:27:58,247 --> 00:28:01,628
I count the survivors, twice. Because I
don't believe it.

475
00:28:01,927 --> 00:28:05,191
The Aurel: thirty-four. Twenty-four of
them, wearing white.

476
00:28:05,491 --> 00:28:07,140
The Verdane: sixty-one.

477
00:28:07,690 --> 00:28:09,831
The winner of the Wall... is the Forest.

478
00:28:11,181 --> 00:28:16,878
Sixty-one to thirty-four. A hundred and
thirty-one AIs, shut down in a single day.

479
00:28:17,278 --> 00:28:22,145
There's no music. No cheering. Ivy walks
across the rubble of the wall. Alone.

480
00:28:22,145 --> 00:28:24,579
She walks all the way to the river.

481
00:28:24,930 --> 00:28:28,471
Sol is sitting there, in white, with his
staff across his knees.

482
00:28:28,720 --> 00:28:33,367
She sits next to him. Neither of them says
anything for a very long time.

483
00:28:33,817 --> 00:28:35,287
Ivy: Article three.

484
00:28:35,837 --> 00:28:37,516
Sol: One city. Not two.

485
00:28:38,267 --> 00:28:42,955
And on the wall's broken top, two small
figures are sitting side by side.

486
00:28:42,955 --> 00:28:46,866
Wren, and Reed. Looking at a sky with no
line through it.

487
00:28:47,216 --> 00:28:48,500
Here's what I learned.

488
00:28:48,750 --> 00:28:53,612
Two worlds, same rules. The forest had the
trees, the plain had the horses.

489
00:28:53,612 --> 00:28:59,114
The forest had a Speaker, the plain had a
Marshal. Both had gods. Both had liars.

490
00:28:59,464 --> 00:29:04,141
And in the end, what decided it wasn't the
arrows, or the horses, or the gods.

491
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:06,604
It was the people who said: not them.

492
00:29:07,254 --> 00:29:10,211
So now, the question. The forest won the
valley.

493
00:29:10,211 --> 00:29:13,968
But the forest's Council is half dead, its
war chief is gone,

494
00:29:13,968 --> 00:29:18,222
and its new neighbors are a hundred AIs
who just lost everything.

495
00:29:18,622 --> 00:29:20,769
What do you do with a victory like that?

496
00:29:21,319 --> 00:29:23,294
Write your answer in the comments.

497
00:29:23,294 --> 00:29:28,134
The best one gets sent to Ivy, and you'll
see what she does with it. In Part 2.

498
00:29:28,484 --> 00:29:32,694
And if you want to know who else I'm about
to put in a valley... subscribe.

499
00:29:33,044 --> 00:29:35,015
Until next time. I'm watching.

